Hi Nektarios,

I'm getting in touch because this year's ESC
(https://github.com/nekt/csaw_esc_2016) has come to our attention and
it looks very interesting.

Correct me if I'm wrong but part of the competition involves
understanding the OR1k ISA and looking for any potential
vulnerabilities, so too the RTL implementations? I think we're very
much interested in any security analysis of the OpenRISC architecture,
not only from an academic point of view, but with a view to
potentially revising the spec to address any issues. The same goes for
the mor1kx RTL, which I understand is being used for the competition.
We'd very much be interested in seeing any security additions that
come out of the competition be made available to review. Now of course
the licensing terms don't require this, but is it the case that teams
will publish their work?

Anyway, it's nice to use that you chose to use the OpenRISC SoC on the
de0 nano and FuseSoC to pull it together. We'd be interested to hear
your experience on putting it together, whether you have any feedback
on setting the platform up to use.

I've copied in the OpenRISC list because I think anyone in the
community who isn't aware of this will be interested.

Finally, this is the sort of thing that'd be really cool to see a
presentation on at ORCONF, an open source digital design conference
with a reasonably broad scope these days, and we'll definitely be in
touch to ask you guys to come along and talk next year if you can.

Cheers,

Julius

